## QC review

Blank-context reviewer returned `VERDICT: findings` with 2 findings, **both self-labeled
UNVERIFIED** by the reviewer itself. Both dismissed on inspection of code outside the diff:
`telegram.route.ts:19-23` and `app.ts:266-270` catch init-data errors with an unconditional
`reply.code(401)` and no message matching, so the new error message cannot surface as a 500 at
either endpoint. The same risk class was real at the 4 sites that *do* match on message
strings (`profile.route.ts` x1, `provider.route.ts` x3) and the diff handles all 4. Full
adjudication with line references in `reports/TASK-010-qc-review-cycle1.md`. No redispatch needed.

## Two things the Auditor should look at

1. **`profile.route.ts` and `provider.route.ts` were touched, and the brief named
   `profile.route.ts` as out of scope.** I judged this in-scope and correct, but it is a
   judgement call and I am flagging it rather than burying it. The brief's exclusion was about
   that route's *POST-body initData contract*, which is untouched. What changed is 4 lines
   adding the new `"future-dated telegram init data"` message alongside the existing
   `"stale telegram init data"` in each 401 status mapping. Without it, a future-dated token
   would 500 instead of 401 at those routes — the change is required for item 4 to be correct,
   and is the same caller-contract wiring the brief explicitly demanded for item 1's upload error.

2. **A pre-existing test-isolation flake, reported not fixed (out of scope).** `apps/api` tests
   share the gitignored `apps/api/.runtime-artifacts` directory as mutable on-disk state.
   Concurrent test files race in `hydrateArtifactsFromDisk` (`report.service.ts:226`), producing
   intermittent ENOENT failures that grow more frequent as that directory accumulates. My first
   verification run showed 1 failure and my second showed 4 — which is why the "390/390" claim
   needs the qualifier that follows.

   **I proved this is pre-existing, not introduced**: with all TASK-010 changes stashed, baseline
   runs gave 373/373, then 372/373 (1 failed), then 373/373. The affected code path is untouched
   by this ticket.

   **Honest statement of the green**: the suite is 390/390 deterministically *when
   `apps/api/.runtime-artifacts` is cleared first*. Without clearing, any run of the full suite
   may show unrelated ENOENT failures. This matters beyond this ticket — it makes "full API suite
   green" (an acceptance criterion of this build, and a TASK-008 gate input) non-deterministic as
   currently run. Recorded as a finding on TASK-010; suggest a dedicated ticket alongside TASK-012.

## Process note

The engineer's envelope placed its evidence at the envelope's schema-required top level, but the
merge engine only merges keys under `proposed_changes`, so the first merge (rev 5) left
`task.evidence` empty. I merged a second orchestrator envelope (rev 6) carrying my own verified
evidence in the correct location. No hand-editing of the record at any point; both envelopes went
through the engine and validated. Worth fixing in the brief template.

Budget: cycle completed in roughly 35 minutes of the 2-hour ticket allowance.
